\name{run_parity}
\alias{run_parity}
\title{Run the cross-implementation parity suite}
\usage{
run_parity(vec_path, verbose = TRUE)
}
\arguments{
\item{vec_path}{path to \code{vectors.json}, generated by the reference
implementation's \code{parity/gen_vectors.py}.}
\item{verbose}{print per-scenario results.}
}
\value{a list with per-scenario failure counts, \code{values_checked},
\code{structure_ok}, and total \code{fails}.}
\description{
The assertion engine behind both test harnesses (\code{tests/parity.R} and the
testthat suite): 55 scenarios checked against the Python-generated vectors at
a tolerance of 1e-6, plus the candidate-population structure block. Primarily
for development and continuous integration.
}
\keyword{internal}
